<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea yields close down on brisk sentiment.</title>
<headline>S.Korea yields close down on brisk sentiment.</headline>
<text>
<p>Yields on three-year benchmark corporate bonds finished lower for the fourth straight day this week on strong buying from institutional investors, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Three-month CD yields also fell the lowest level since July 29 on the back of scanty new issues.</p>
<p>* 3-yr corporates close at 12.00 vs 12.04 pct</p>
<p>* 3-mth CDs end at 13.30 vs 13.45</p>
<p>* Overnight average call rates unchanged at 14.5</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
</text>
